From 8580981488d6065cb40d2eddf516ca221b866efc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 13:51:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dashboard: the rail clock gets its red seconds back
 (regression, v3.0.9)

Owner report 2026-09-07: the seconds in the dashboard's clock are no longer
crimson, while every other page shows them correctly.

Cause, exactly. v3.0.9 (d1ed232aa0) removed "five orphaned style blocks after a
cross-page usage check (arrow, railsearch, rc-sec, spark, speeds)" from
Main_ReaperDash.asp. Four of those five really were dead. `.rc-sec` was not: the
span that carries it is written at RUNTIME by /js/reaper_clock.js (tk(), the
innerHTML line), which this page loads, so the class appears nowhere inside the
page and an in-file usage check calls it orphaned. It only became invisible to
such a check in v2.9.4 (4387547afa), which moved the clock's inline script out
to that shared file. reaper_shell.asp keeps its own copy of the rule and was not
part of that sweep - which is why the shell-drawn pages kept red seconds and the
dashboard, which draws its own topbar, did not. Shipped in every image from
v3.0.9 (2026-09-04) onward.

The rule is restored next to .rc-time, matching reaper_shell.asp, with a comment
saying why it must never be swept again. Re-checked the other four against every
.js the dashboard loads (reaper_clock.js, reaper_util.js): still genuinely dead,
left removed.

Verified: --crimson is defined on the page; the rail clock rendered from this
page's own :root + .railclock CSS with the exact markup the script emits shows
bone seconds before and crimson after. reaper_static_checks 11/11, page ASCII.
CSS only - no script, no token, no dict change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/www/Main_ReaperDash.asp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/release/src/router/www/Main_ReaperDash.asp b/release/src/router/www/Main_ReaperDash.asp
index 5dd4f628c3..7b3f2885be 100644
--- a/release/src/router/www/Main_ReaperDash.asp
+++ b/release/src/router/www/Main_ReaperDash.asp
@@ -77,6 +77,12 @@ main{min-width:0}
   display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding:14px 12px 14px;gap:2px}
 .railclock{padding:6px 6px 14px;text-align:center;line-height:1.05}
 .railclock .rc-time{font-family:var(--hdr);font-weight:700;font-size:23px;letter-spacing:.07em;color:var(--bone);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
+/* The seconds are crimson. NOT ORPHANED, do not sweep it again: the span carrying
+   this class is emitted at RUNTIME by /js/reaper_clock.js (tk(), the innerHTML line),
+   which this page loads - so it appears nowhere in this file. v3.0.9 removed it on an
+   in-file usage check and the dashboard clock lost its red seconds while every other
+   page, drawn by reaper_shell.asp, kept them (owner report 2026-09-07). */
+.railclock .rc-sec{color:var(--crimson)}
 .railclock .rc-date{font-family:var(--hdr);font-weight:600;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--steel);margin-top:4px}
